SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Hot Chocolate ***\n
 Spanish Hot Chocolate — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, 
 Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elas
 tics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: H
 igh Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply found
 ation and powder matching skintone\n• Light skin tone eye shadow over 
 entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• Medium brown eye 
 shadow blended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara
  to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner af
 ter lashes dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so danc
 er doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on c
 ontour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to da
 rken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may we
 ar flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelin
 es:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damag
 e to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event 
 of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\
 n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes
  by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in
  costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any co
 stume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and s
 hall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during 
 its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while 
 in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• 
 Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the ex
 ception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressin
 g rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure he
 ad pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to the
 ir assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Ar
 kansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored 
 drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
