SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Notes (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nTime: 9:00 PM–9:30 PM.\nIn Performance Co
 stumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDIN
 G RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and ba
 ckstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals 
 (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehea
 rsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\n
 SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and 
 the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/s
 preadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTU
 ME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Hot Chocolate ***\nSpanish Hot Chocolate — Cost
 ume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; 
 Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancac
 ked)\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage 
 Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundation and powder matching skin
 tone\n• Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye
  shadow over crease\n• Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•
  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before applicat
 ion of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Blush on t
 he cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out i
 n the stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n
 • Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or 
 Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh
  tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces
  with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Pro
 mptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point
  of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or a
 ccessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• 
 Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt t
 o alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never 
 apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrai
 n from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from 
 the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any
  garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food 
 or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not r
 emove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n
 • Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following 
 their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply 
 fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n
 • Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may d
 amage or stain costumes.
