SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B @ 2:30 PM – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory – Pro
 duction Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 2:45 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 2:30 PM.\nOn stage: 3:30 PM–4:20 PM.\nACT II
  Cast B Performance.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RUL
 ES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backsta
 ge - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st 
 Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals
  and Performances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJE
 CT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the B
 A portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spread
 sheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / 
 HAIR / MAKEUP — Hot Chocolate ***\nSpanish Hot Chocolate — Costume (
 you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes
 : Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\
 ; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeu
 p Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\
 n• Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shad
 ow over crease\n• Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n• Blac
 k fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application o
 f fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Blush on the ch
 eeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the
  stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• U
 se a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark 
 Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone
  ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with
  care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly
  notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of d
 iscovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or access
 ories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refra
 in from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alt
 er\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply
  stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain fro
 m smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the u
 se of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garm
 ent not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or be
 verage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove
  costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Re
 move all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their 
 use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully 
 with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do
  not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage 
 or stain costumes.
